# ── resumebuilder-worker — Docker build context ────────────────────────
# The build context is this directory, so anything listed here is neither sent to the daemon nor
# available to a COPY. Two of these are not merely size optimisations:
#
#   * `.env` — the real environment file. `COPY` is explicit in the Dockerfile so it would not be
#     picked up by accident today, but a future `COPY . .` would bake production secrets into a
#     layer. Excluding it here makes that mistake impossible rather than unlikely.
#   * `.git` — this directory is now its own repository, so the context would otherwise carry the
#     whole object database on every build.
#
# `node_modules` and `dist` are excluded because the image installs and compiles its own: a host
# `node_modules` built on macOS/arm64 would be copied over the Linux one and break the runtime.

# ── Dependencies ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules
npm-debug.log*

# ── Build output ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
dist
build
*.tsbuildinfo

# ── Environment files ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ── Version control ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.gitignore

# ── Documentation and repo metadata ────────────────────────────────────
*.md
.github
LICENSE
.editorconfig

# ── Tests and coverage ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
tests
coverage
vitest.config.ts

# ── Local data / logs / scratch ────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
*.bson
*.wt
*.tmp
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej

# ── Tool / IDE caches ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
.claude
.shipstudio
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
